issue(id="0014" status="open")
  title Design importer intent profiles and unify the API shape
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of puggers
    i-want the importer's user-facing API to describe coherent intents instead of only exposing a growing pile of low-level flags
    so-that CLI, library, and future npm users can ask for the kind of view they want without reverse-engineering every knob
  premise.
    Once baseline corrections, whitespace policy, and initial compatibility work
    are in place, the remaining question is product shape: should users choose
    profiles such as readable-document, structure-inspection, or preserve-more,
    or should they assemble everything from low-level flags, or both? That
    question should be answered after the underlying semantics are more stable,
    not before. This task is about defining the user-facing behavior matrix and
    making sure the same model can be explained across CLI, library, and future
    npm surfaces.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Decide whether importer intent should surface as named profiles, composable low-level flags, or a layered model that supports both, and document the reasoning.
    criterion Define at least two concrete importer intents with example option mappings and example output differences.
    criterion Ensure the resulting API shape can be represented consistently across CLI, library, and future npm surfaces without each surface inventing its own semantics.
    criterion Add or update tests, help text, or documentation so the chosen API shape is visible in repo artifacts rather than only captured in task prose.
    criterion Keep the behavior matrix small enough that new users can predict the major tradeoffs without reading every implementation detail.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Decide whether profiles should be stable user-facing promises or just convenience aliases over lower-level options.
    item(status="open") Confirm that the API shape reflects real user intents from `0007` rather than abstract taxonomy work.
    item(status="open") Make sure future surfaces can adopt the same model incrementally without waiting for every importer option to stabilize first.
